Feature addition: enable bloom with high threshold for neon glow effect.

This commit modifies 7 files (+13/-13 lines), spanning 5 TypeScript source, 1 game entities, 1 networking.
This feature extends the Geometry Wars 3D codebase with new functionality. The implementation follows the project's established patterns and maintains compatibility with both single-player and multiplayer code paths where applicable.

Additional context from the commit body:
Fix the white-out issue by raising bloom threshold to 0.85 so only
bright entity pixels bloom (not the grid at ~0.64 brightness).
Switch persistent additive effects to NormalBlending to prevent
accumulated brightness from exceeding threshold:
- GlowTrail: 4 layered lines were the worst offender
- EntityGlow: sprite halos
- Geom glow lines
- WeaponPickup glow sprites

Bloom params: strength=1.0, radius=0.4, threshold=0.85
Enabled across all three entry points (main, multiplayer, network).

Key files: src/effects/EntityGlow.ts, src/effects/GlowTrail.ts, src/entities/Geom.ts, src/main.ts, src/multiplayer-main.ts, and others.
